        "original_id": "7251cd1c-1b9f-58ba-91f3-367759744090",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Zhaoqing, Kangding, Guangdong Province, Sichuan province, Southwest China\n- Organizations: Garzê Tibetan Autonomous Prefecture\n- Systems: Guangzhou–Maoming Railway\n- Topics: Population, urban areas, romanization\n\nFacts:\n- Zhaoqing was formerly romanized as Shiuhing.\n- Zhaoqing is a prefecture-level city in Guangdong Province, China.\n- During the 2010 census, Zhaoqing had a population of 3,918,467.\n- During the 2010 census, 1,232,462 people in Zhaoqing lived in the urbanized areas of Duanzhou District and Gaoyao County.\n- Kangding, also known as Dartsedo in Tibetan, is a city in western Sichuan province of Southwest China.\n- Kangding is the seat of Garzê Tibetan Autonomous Prefecture.\n- Kangding's urban center has around 100,000 inhabitants.\n- The Guangzhou–Maoming Railway runs through Guangzhou, Sanshui, Zhaoqing, Xinxing County, Yangchun, and Maoming.",
